From: Nicholas Carlini <nicholas@carlini.com>
Date: Tue, 31 Mar 2026 15:25:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] eventpoll: defer struct eventpoll free to RCU grace period

In certain situations, ep_free() in eventpoll.c will kfree the epi->ep
eventpoll struct while it still being used by another concurrent thread.
Defer the kfree() to an RCU callback to prevent UAF.

Fixes: f2e467a48287 ("eventpoll: Fix semi-unbounded recursion")
Signed-off-by: Nicholas Carlini <nicholas@carlini.com>
Signed-off-by: Christian Brauner <brauner@kernel.org>

diff --git a/fs/eventpoll.c b/fs/eventpoll.c
index 5714e900567c..4b43bf41296d 100644
--- a/fs/eventpoll.c
+++ b/fs/eventpoll.c
@@ -226,6 +226,9 @@ struct eventpoll {
 	 */
 	refcount_t refcount;

+	/* used to defer freeing past ep_get_upwards_depth_proc() RCU walk */
+	struct rcu_head rcu;
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_NET_RX_BUSY_POLL
 	/* used to track busy poll napi_id */
 	unsigned int napi_id;
@@ -819,7 +822,8 @@ static void ep_free(struct eventpoll *ep)
 	mutex_destroy(&ep->mtx);
 	free_uid(ep->user);
 	wakeup_source_unregister(ep->ws);
-	kfree(ep);
+	/* ep_get_upwards_depth_proc() may still hold epi->ep under RCU */
+	kfree_rcu(ep, rcu);
 }

 /*
-- 
2.34.1

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
kfree(ep);
rcu_read_lock();
rcu_read_unlock();
```
Reason:
`ep_free()` calls `kfree(ep)` immediately, without waiting for an RCU grace period. Meanwhile, another thread may be within an RCU read-side critical section (e.g., in `ep_get_upwards_depth_proc()`) that accesses `epi->ep`. Because `ep_free()` frees the `eventpoll` structure while the reader still holds a reference, a use-after-free occurs.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
+	struct rcu_head rcu;
-	kfree(ep);
+	kfree_rcu(ep, rcu);
```
Reason:
Adding a `struct rcu_head` field to `eventpoll` enables deferred freeing via `kfree_rcu()`. Replacing `kfree(ep)` with `kfree_rcu(ep, rcu)` ensures the structure is freed only after an RCU grace period, so that any concurrent RCU readers (such as those in `ep_get_upwards_depth_proc()`) have finished accessing `epi->ep` before the memory is reclaimed. This prevents the use-after-free.

